<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Nan Ya Jan-Aug sales slide.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Nan Ya Jan-Aug sales slide.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nan Ya Plastics Corp, Taiwan's largest industrial enterprise, said on Tuesday its combined sales revenues between January and August fell 5.3 percent to T$57.689 billion from the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>In the month of August, Nan Ya's sales were down 1.7 percent to T$7.39 billion, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement gave no profit figures.</p>
<p>Nan Ya has set a sales target of T$98.35 billion for 1996.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
